{"chunk_id": "934ce7ea3611", "text": "In the thirty\u2011sixth year after the Kurukshetra war, ominous signs appear across the world. News soon reaches the Pandavas that the Yadava clans\u2014Vrishnis, Andhakas, and Bhojas\u2014have destroyed themselves. The calamity traces back to a curse: when the Yadavas mock visiting sages, they are told that Samba will give birth to an iron bolt that will annihilate their race. Though the bolt is ground to powder and cast into the sea, fate unfolds. At Prabhasa, drunken quarrels erupt among the Yadava heroes; blades of grass transform into iron bolts and they slaughter one another. Balarama departs through yogic transformation, Krishna is later struck by the hunter Jara, and Dvaraka falls. Arjuna rescues the survivors but finds his divine power fading, signaling the end of the heroic age.\nCursed fate destroys the Yadava clan in drunken infighting; Balarama departs as a serpent, Krishna is accidentally shot by a hunter and ascends to heaven.\nThemes: inevitable fate, curse and retribution, end of the Yadavas, omens and apocalypse, divine departure", "vector": [-0.010252994485199451, -0.038568828254938126, 0.000389033870305866, 0.009745148941874504, -0.023649141192436218, 0.007205919828265905, -0.03266683593392372, -0.01922951079905033, -0.01836480014026165, -0.009484362788498402, 0.020560890436172485, 0.006471602246165276, 0.011049076914787292, 0.01944912038743496, 0.005795618053525686, 0.009347107261419296, 0.036619797348976135, -0.017349109053611755, 0.04139629378914833, 0.00034785718889907, 0.012119670398533344, 0.0023590808268636465, 0.00884612463414669, 0.0014231691602617502, -0.02261972427368164, 0.029207995161414146, 0.012977518141269684, -0.02193344756960869, 0.011906924657523632, -0.007926511578261852, -0.007017193362116814, -0.00416227662935853, -0.004450513049960136, -0.0009376273956149817, -0.03066290356218815, -0.003084819996729493, 0.003343889955431223, -0.02565307356417179, 0.01476870384067297, -0.001768881687894